{"title":"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle of maximal area is inscribed in the region bounded by the graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/f/3cf4746a4f1696224b7047e033e5267c07b0db59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-x^2 -7x + 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" /> and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis. The radius of this circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/2/0328412e6929ed52e228701766bb74d4051cc707.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{p} + q}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d08ff3681d6992f69ee41e21c7237c89f970ac49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A permutation of the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/6/b16c8124946e3b6f7abcf9534dbce7d80a14a192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/087594ea26fa196b8e61bc20a36228270dc695f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/c/3ac4b608f7c3628c4c6fb7263c268c87ea70e2d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"18\" /> is called <i>golden</i> if every two consecutive numbers in the permutation are relatively prime. How many <i>golden</i> permutations are there?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems/Problem 2\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/e/e9e12eefbe37a0e96fda2ca5040de907d7abf0e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MNO$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec6a580e5f5a9d4701dc20725a4d9eb9bcf85f87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"77\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/2/3e25b835068a12215078af19243edcf741e50866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$NO=21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/5/ea54dc3fce33a21edbb123db7d911abf207be4c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MO=23$\" width=\"75\" height=\"12\" />. The trisection points of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/e/4fe8176d34b11c58cdf7b40a9decdb390f934318.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MO$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/7/3e7a4a71a486f6995df17b527737fa5c6586616d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ME&lt;MF$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"92\" height=\"13\" />. Segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5bf33c0fc6f66ddf042e950c5f4711c78f9d387.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$NE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/c/a4c083d125a1e4c47b9714a67f005e993055eed5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$NF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> are extended to points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411ef29ce6c32ab71534dfd3319a6fe72af9c5ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/7/6d794967bd855edced950369620307257fee99f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F&#39;$\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/8/548c5b02de61d88798e244b479275ad72164d038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ME&#39; || NF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/5020418eab4561edfcbe7fab23d49380344a608e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OF&#39; || NE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />. The area of pentagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/d/80db2f4b474af8dd18407fb30220e3508e069d2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MNOF&#39;E&#39;$\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/e/8aee7d8c78ae43dcfbc54f153dd3036efe008b64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\sqrt{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/0/170200756543596efeb46fca1cf29a617e8c9192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems/Problem 3\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/8/08882710472f6455a5e628f0b8ae55349481d0aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x)=3x^2+2x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"19\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/c/58c2927fb7f8991d6d1c1ae59ec3b0e70cccb20e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^n (x) = p(p^{n-1}(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/5/9453c4c0399c9140b63f3d3f2bd06bada4225358.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^1 (x) = p(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"19\" />. The product of the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/a/20ab4ca83ab79bc5ea1c0e0d5760988233e97827.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^5 (x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"19\" /> can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/524d9b869d9ee2d8b923afa9ce7c2c36bd9489e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"18\" height=\"33\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems/Problem 4\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define a triple inequality to be an inequality of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/e/51e3c884a9a0fe6eb0f33495debd2423f925df1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_i &gt; r_j &gt; r_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"14\" />. Bradley has a list of 50 real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/8/5f881b9de9eda22511b2d10fa8679c120304031d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r_1, r_2, \\cdots, r_{50})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />, but he will only give Batra triple inequalities consisting of 3 numbers in the list. For example, if Bradley gives Batra only the triple inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/a/98ad2106858a5652f994538801d3cfe8c3192b2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_7 &gt; r_2 &gt; r_{49}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"100\" height=\"12\" />, Batra knows that the 7th number is greater than the 2nd number which is greater than the 49th number, but nothing else. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the maximum number of (distinct) triple inequalities that Bradley could give Batra such that Batra cannot determine the order of the full list of 50 numbers. Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by 1000.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems/Problem 5\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Eli has 5 strings.  He begins by taking one end of one of the strings, and tying it to another end of a string (possibly the same string) chosen at random.  He continues on by tying two randomly selected untied ends together until there are no more untied ends, and only loops remain.  The expected value of the number of loops that he will have in the end can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/084079bf1d54500f3c59257a7ec3467932b72ba2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"34\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are relatively prime positive integers.  Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems/Problem 6\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let two circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3e233bb1da8d66bebec90849a037a8f32147ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1, O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> with radii <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17fd2cd9f6e99b1cb8a62451cc12bbf2afe22b0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3, 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> in the plane be centered at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/0/ec00004a5113b974f70a8e26c3781261e56464e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M, N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, respectively. Consider a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in the plane such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/f/b7ffd20d408a3f67877b051b433a592997c91975.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PM = \\sqrt{33}, PN = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"163\" height=\"20\" />. Denote the intersections of the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/8/80879b243f734e54b71362c7486c965353c210f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3216e8846eb44f1055c322fb5bd30169d5d62cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef747a48a2a8d43c4841e12c89f2de2502a672e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" />, and the intersections of the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/f/99f9b09eac5bb37f279692c70f4e8a80ff2b787d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PN$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee48e5d3968014ef1e27c31e56d2f7ea5f8cb1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/7/1375da8b94d688b4928311f04d35a57081ee0f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C, D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3216e8846eb44f1055c322fb5bd30169d5d62cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee48e5d3968014ef1e27c31e56d2f7ea5f8cb1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> intersect at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/8/788f3c8df73c43990991c6f116e759e1e1116b47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X, Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"16\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/e/aae09d4486fc00fff609a7fe5436325c57e18b5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> equals the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/7/4672d071da959cfdd45124e5a4169f350e8d2e55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{PMN}$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/1/3e1331a55db2e3939fac59e4485878d818545e97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"31\" height=\"13\" /> can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37e15f1d23ccbfb0d5d98110998b16533e80271e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\sqrt{b}+c\\sqrt{d}+e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"117\" height=\"19\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/7/f67f4a1dfe3f757a6e0ba16ce1f5c6b3ed25049d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b, d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> are distinct squarefree integers. Find  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78e9da7691c4a59208721a2da0f7bbc510d639fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c+d+e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems/Problem 7\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that the complex number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/b/05b1ac9f729910eeb585972547f596db1efe0224.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left|z\\right| = \\left|z^2+1\\right|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"101\" height=\"22\" />.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> is the maximum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/7/a37d345c5c4dc4bd651c7f87a5e7396ec9ec2d0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left|z\\right|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"21\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/f/fbf54eac904c649c577ad3fb7c9cbaa0c0090fb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K^4$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/3/ec32b83c7b36e6db008f7c885a292dcf5235c663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{r+\\sqrt{s}}{t}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"57\" height=\"39\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/4/3b4d8cb6aa374535cea16c712b70c8f6ba8155ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r+s+t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems/Problem 8\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A class of seven students is doing a Secret Santa, for which all seven students have contributed a gift each. However, one of the seven students has not arrived yet. The teacher decides to randomly assign each of the six students present to a gift that is not their own. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the probability that the seventh student is left with his own gift once he arrives, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/9/b99d4c98e3405156d8c293d3a4c546ff50c04d07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor1000P\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems/Problem 9\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/e/ffebeca0e9e5450549bf8fa6fd67992c488d1626.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n,x) = \\dfrac{\\sin{x} + \\sin{2x} + \\sin{3x} + \\cdots + \\sin{(n-1)x} + \\sin{nx}}{\\cos{x} + \\cos{2x} + \\cos{3x} + \\cdots + \\cos{(n-1)x} + \\cos{nx}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"487\" height=\"43\" />. Find the sum of all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/9/9c99e559f442ef0aa3fa82520660fbf6a2d52939.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(23,x)=f(33,x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is measured in degrees and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/2/2b2633d13f4b43fe48505be4c3666e30c23381a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100&lt;x&lt;200$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"112\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems/Problem 10\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> has sides of length 13, 14, and 15. Set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is the set of all points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> for which the circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times. The points in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> enclose a finite region whose area can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cb1c437204427e39d2a330294b9970133d8b48e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{p-q\\pi}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"53\" height=\"33\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d08ff3681d6992f69ee41e21c7237c89f970ac49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> be a polynomial of degree 10 satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/f/1cfebcfc94c75e54ec78610add62e6d15ad13248.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x^2) = P(x)P(x-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"177\" height=\"19\" />. Find the maximum possible sum of the coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems/Problem 12\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Eduardo and Silvie play the Factor Game. Eduardo initially picks a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />; Silvie then subtracts a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/065e6d116d16109a19d183a52f7714325b6be623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N&#39;$\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Eduardo then subtracts a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/065e6d116d16109a19d183a52f7714325b6be623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N&#39;$\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/065e6d116d16109a19d183a52f7714325b6be623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N&#39;$\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/1/7c13d39ab20ccae979801ae7fb6010144db996ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N&#39;&#39;$\" width=\"24\" height=\"14\" /> and so on. Neither player is allowed to subtract 1 at any time. The loser is the person who must subtract a number from itself and get zero. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of all positive integers less than 1000 which Eduardo can choose as the initial number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> to ensure that he wins (assuming optimal play). Find the remainder when the sum of the elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by 1000.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems/Problem 13\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of complex numbers of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/b/69b5d9cfbac40e0d795398b0648b92ed41ca48ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+di$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c59cc6a2f6821e94b390834eb8f628bf5b452ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+di = (a+bi)^{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"19\" /> for some integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. Find the largest integer that must divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for all numbers in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems/Problem 14\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Paula the Painter initially paints every complex number black. When Paula toggles a complex number, she paints it white if it was previously black, and black if it was previously white. For each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/f/3bf5d1704ec64876bcc683e890a4b8baaa1aa60c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1,2,\\dots,20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"118\" height=\"16\" />, Paula progressively toggles the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/d/7fd2354774a784e9e9fc82cec0e94acce53413c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2k}+x^k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"17\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of complex numbers are white at the end of this process. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems/Problem 15\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018001215\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.064 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.077 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 675/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/209